The source code is licensed under Apache-2.0. Model weights and source datasets
are separate artifacts with their own terms.

Qwen3.5-0.8B is developed by the Qwen team at Alibaba Cloud and is licensed under
Apache-2.0. Dohnuts trains language LoRA adapters and a decision head over this
base. Base weights are downloaded from the original publisher.
https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.5-0.8B

The RLCD objective and evaluation protocols follow Laya by Nandha Kishor M and
Laya Vision by Reed Richards. Both projects are licensed under Apache-2.0.
Pinned references and implementation details are recorded in docs/rlcd.md and
docs/upstream-alignment.md.
https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya
https://github.com/r33drichards/laya-vision

JevBench supplies the public benchmark tasks and scoring protocol. Published Jev
outcomes are reference measurements, not locally executed Jev predictions.
https://github.com/fstandhartinger/jevbench

Bub supplies the agent SDK. Flash Linear Attention supplies fused operators.
They are installed as dependencies, not bundled copies of their source code.
https://github.com/bubbuild/bub
https://github.com/fla-org/flash-linear-attention

Dataset sources, provenance, and terms are listed in docs/data-and-evaluation.md.
Raw datasets, source images, and third-party model weights are not distributed
with this source repository or Python package. Reference names do not imply
endorsement by their authors.
